# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root .dockerignore
#
# Both apps/api/Dockerfile and apps/web/Dockerfile are built with the repo
# root as build context (`docker build -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .`), so this
# file governs what's available to COPY in *both* images. Keep it broad:
# smaller build context = faster `docker build` (less to send to the daemon)
# and no chance of secrets/dev artifacts accidentally ending up in a layer.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version control / editor / agent metadata
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude
.agents
.mcp.json
.vscode
.idea

# Dependencies (always reinstalled inside the image via pnpm)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output (always rebuilt inside the image)
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
build
**/build
coverage
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Env files / secrets — never bake these into an image. Images are pulled by
# runtime config (compose env, k8s secrets, etc.), not baked-in .env files.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Logs
*.log
**/*.log
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Docs — irrelevant to the build, only bloats build-context transfer
*.md
**/*.md

# Local Postgres bootstrap + compose (not part of either app image)
docker
docker-compose.yml

# Misc
.DS_Store
skills-lock.json
